@startuml
title S-CORE Lifecycle Collector | Class Diagram (LLD)
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #4F5D75
skinparam classBorderColor #2D3142
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classFontColor #2D3142
skinparam classAttributeFontColor #2D3142
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #BFC0C0
skinparam packageBorderColor #2D3142
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam packageFontColor #2D3142

package "VEL Evidence Ingestion (S-CORE State Collection)" {

  package "Collector Hierarchy" {
    abstract class SourceCollector {
      +collector_id : string
      +source_ref : string
      +collection_trigger : CollectionTrigger
      +collection_window : object
      +parameters : object
      +collect() : Result<vector<RawStateRecord>, CollectorError>
      +get_metadata() : collection_metadata
      +get_diagnostics() : diagnostics
      +health_probe() : health_status
    }

    class SCoreCollector {
      +source_ref : string = "score.<module>"
      +collector_id : string = "<module>-collector"
      +transport : Transport = s-core-api
    }

    SourceCollector <|-- SCoreCollector : extends

    note right of SourceCollector
      • Common VEL collector interface (all source categories)
      • I/O API per source-collector-interface-design.md Sec 3
      • Lifecycle state machine per Sec 4.1
      • Error taxonomy per Sec 5.1
    end note

    note right of SCoreCollector
      • S-CORE conventions on SourceCollector (CONCRETE)
      • Naming: source_ref=score.<module>, collector_id=<module>-collector
      • Transport: s-core-api
      • One generic class; each S-CORE module = configured instance
        (Lifecycle: source_ref=score.lifecycle, collector_id=lifecycle-collector)
      • Binding realization (generic vs. plugin) selected via
        fieldBindingProvider config
    end note
  }

  package "Shared Engine" {
    interface IStateFieldBindingProvider {
      +field_names() : list<string>
      +read_field(field_name : string) : any
      +subscribe(on_update : callback) : bool
    }

    class PluginLoader {
      +load(fieldBindingProvider config) : IStateFieldBindingProvider*
      +unload(provider : IStateFieldBindingProvider*) : void
    }

    class ConfigDrivenStateMapper {
      -schema_ref : RawEvidenceSchema
      +map_to_raw_record(bindings : IStateFieldBindingProvider) : object
      +validate_required_fields() : bool
      +apply_field_conversions() : void
    }

    class CollectorDiagnostics {
      +error_code : string
      +error_category : ErrorCategory
      +severity : Severity
      +message : string
      +retry_count : uint32
      +recovery_hint : string
      +emit() : AdapterDiagnostic
    }

    SCoreCollector ..> IStateFieldBindingProvider : uses (resolved by PluginLoader\nfrom lifecycle-collector.yaml's\nfieldBindingProvider config)
    SCoreCollector ..> ConfigDrivenStateMapper : uses
    SCoreCollector ..> CollectorDiagnostics : reports via
    ConfigDrivenStateMapper ..> IStateFieldBindingProvider : reads fields via
    PluginLoader ..> IStateFieldBindingProvider : instantiates

    note right of IStateFieldBindingProvider
      • Shared engine (collapsed); see Collector_common_class_diagram.puml
      • Lifecycle realization = external plugin (LifecycleFieldBindings)
      • read_field()/subscribe() return RAW native values; enum conversion
        done by ConfigDrivenStateMapper (via schema `conversion` block)
    end note

    note right of PluginLoader
      • Loads plugin from lifecycle-collector.yaml (kind: plugin);
        resolves C-ABI entry point, checks ABI version, returns
        IStateFieldBindingProvider*
      • No Lifecycle-specific knowledge (shared by all modules)
    end note
  }

  package "Lifecycle Native Plugin (built & deployed independently of VEL core)" #FFF1E9 {
    class LifecycleFieldBindings <<plugin>> {
      -transport : s-core-api = lifecycle-state-api
      +field_names() : list<string>
      +read_field(field_name : string) : any
      +subscribe(on_update : callback) : bool
    }

    IStateFieldBindingProvider <|.. LifecycleFieldBindings : implements\n(via PluginLoader)

    note right of LifecycleFieldBindings
      • External plugin: built/versioned independently, loaded at
        runtime via lifecycle-collector.yaml (kind: plugin)
      • Exports C-ABI factory/destructor entry points
      • Maintains TWO mw::com connections:
        (1) ILmControl (pull) -- run_target via get_active_run_target()
        (2) IExtMonitorNotify (push) -- ProcessMonitorNotify via
            ext_monitor_notify callback
      • read_field(): returns RAW native values (no enum conversion;
        that's ConfigDrivenStateMapper's job)
      • subscribe(): registers callback; snapshots full payload per
        event generation (atomic swap; no mixing)
      • Only Lifecycle-specific artifact; lives outside VEL core
    end note
  }

  package "Enums" {
    enum CollectionTrigger {
      PERIODIC
      EVENT
      ON_DEMAND
    }

    enum Transport {
      S_CORE_API
      DDS
      FILE
      COMMAND
      OS_INTERFACE
    }

    enum ErrorCategory {
      CONFIGURATION_ERROR
      SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE
      AUTHENTICATION_ERROR
      TIMEOUT
      SCHEMA_VIOLATION
      NORMALIZATION_ERROR
      RESOURCE_EXHAUSTION
      INTERNAL_ERROR
    }

    enum Severity {
      INFO
      WARNING
      ERROR
      FATAL
    }

    enum CollectorLifecycleState {
      PROVISIONED
      ACTIVE
      RUNNING
      SUSPENDED
      ERROR
      TERMINATED
    }

    SourceCollector --> CollectionTrigger : collection_trigger
    SourceCollector --> CollectorLifecycleState : lifecycle state
    SCoreCollector --> Transport : transport
    CollectorDiagnostics --> ErrorCategory : error_category
    CollectorDiagnostics --> Severity : severity
  }
}

package "S-CORE Lifecycle (source-side types)" {
  enum ProcessState {
    kIdle = 0
    kStarting = 1
    kRunning = 2
    kTerminating = 3
    kTerminated = 4
    kFailed = 5
  }

  enum GraphState {
    kSuccess = 0
    kInTransition = 1
    kAborting = 2
    kCancelled = 3
    kUndefinedState = 4
  }

  enum SupervisionStatus {
    kOk = 0
    kFailed = 1
  }

  enum FailedSupervisionType {
    kHeartbeat = 0
    kDeadline = 1
    kLogic = 2
  }

  enum DeadlineError {
    kTooEarly = 0
    kTooLate = 1
  }

  enum HeartbeatError {
    kTooEarly = 0
    kTooLate = 1
    kMultipleHeartbeats = 2
  }

  enum LogicError {
    kInvalidState = 0
    kInvalidTransition = 1
    kUnmappedError = 2
  }

  class ProcessInfoNode {
    +getPid() : osal::ProcessID
    +getState() : ProcessState
    +getTerminationTimeout() : milliseconds
    +getControlClientChannel() : ControlClientChannelP
  }

  note right of ProcessInfoNode
    • INTERNAL Launch Manager daemon class
    • NOT part of ILmControl / mw::com / external VEL access
    • Shown only to document state/pid origin
  end note

  interface ILmControl {
    +get_active_run_target() : RunTargetName
  }

  interface IExtMonitorNotify {
    +subscribe(on_notify : callback) : Result<void>
    +latest() : optional<ProcessMonitorNotify>
  }

  class ProcessMonitorNotify {
    +process_name : string
    +process_group_name : string
    +process_state : ProcessState
    +pid : uint32
    +exit_code : int32
    +supervision_status : SupervisionStatus
    +failed_supervision_type : FailedSupervisionType
    +deadline_error : DeadlineError
    +deadline_error_us : int64
    +heartbeat_error : HeartbeatError
    +logic_error : LogicError
    +failed_supervision_cycles : uint32
    +deadline_violation : bool
    +alive_indication_count : uint32
    +process_execution_error : uint32
    +process_group_id : string
    +recovery_state : string
  }

  note right of ProcessMonitorNotify
    • Payload type for the external monitor notification capability
    • process_name/process_group_name self-identify the subject
      (callback registered once per LifecycleFieldBindings instance)
    • Originates from PHM; delivered via IExtMonitorNotify mw::com event
  end note

  ProcessInfoNode --> ProcessState : getState()
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> SupervisionStatus : supervision_status
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> FailedSupervisionType : failed_supervision_type
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> DeadlineError : deadline_error
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> HeartbeatError : heartbeat_error
  ProcessMonitorNotify --> LogicError : logic_error
}

LifecycleFieldBindings ..> ProcessState : reads (type only, via notification)
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> GraphState : reads (type only, via notification)
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> ProcessMonitorNotify : reads via notification
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> ILmControl : pull (run_target via get_active_run_target)
LifecycleFieldBindings ..> IExtMonitorNotify : push (subscribe for ProcessMonitorNotify)

note bottom of LifecycleFieldBindings
  • Pull (sync, public): ONLY run_target via ILmControl
  • Push (all other fields): via IExtMonitorNotify as
    ProcessMonitorNotify payload
  • state/pid/graph_state NOT exposed via public API (internal
    Launch Manager classes) -- only via push notification
  • See lifecycle-collector-design.md Sec 2.4/6 for full boundary
end note

@enduml